cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use NeuroTCS in your research, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "NeuroTCS / temporalmetric: Citation-locked, fail-closed longitudinal medical AI audit framework"
abstract: >-
  NeuroTCS is a citation-locked, fail-closed framework for auditing the
  temporal coherence of longitudinal medical AI predictions against
  internationally endorsed published clinical guidelines. The framework
  comprises seven engineering pieces: (1) categorical input contract,
  (2) continuous-biomarker input contract with UCUM unit enforcement,
  (3) citation-locked clinical rule packs spanning Alzheimer's disease
  (NIA-AA 2018, AA 2024), Parkinson's disease (Hoehn-Yahr / MDS-UPDRS),
  multiple sclerosis (McDonald 2024 / EDSS), oncology (RECIST 1.1, iRECIST),
  stroke (modified Rankin Scale), and lung-nodule surveillance (Fleischner
  2017), (4) audit core library (cTCS / pTCS / uTCS with cluster bootstrap
  and Huber M-estimation), (5) FHIR Observation output schema, (6) reference
  dataset adapters (ADNI, PPMI, RIDER, MIRIAD, OASIS-3, ALZ-NET), and
  (7) synthetic-trajectory validation harness. Pieces 1-3 are shipped in
  v1.1.0 with real-world validation on 12,006 ADNI clinical-label transitions
  (65 flagged, 0.54%, all clinically interpretable). Pieces 4-7 are planned.
